Z||000000||chris6878||05-07-2000||10:30 PM||||Well...  first of all, a 15 minute job turned out to be more than expected today. I raised the rear of my fiero, got under and tightened my AC belt. Problem fixed, i now have air. After getting ready to clean up i noticed a small puddle on my work mat under the car. It was gas. One of the main lines "rubber part" was leaking. Good thing i seen this or my fiero may have been toast in the future.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Well.. i fix this problem with a spare fuel line from my parts car. I had to remove the upper plenum on my v6 to get the line i had to remove, kind of tight spot. I put everything back together and she starts up fine and i let her run a while. While she was running i was messing around in the engine area and accidently unplugged the map sensor, and she sputtered and quit. And guess what?  she wont start at all...  doesnt seem to be getting any fire to the plugs?              hope it didnt do something to the ecm (its not 6 months old)<P>any ideas?||||reg||5
